# tools/s/standing_equipment_scope_rank_witness.rish -- what each scope-map row saves, and which
# row to write next.
#
# WHY THIS RUNG. The roster pass is the largest recurring workload on this pier -- 160 guards in
# 1,074 seconds, measured 20260907 across eight ships, four fifths of which never skips
# (external-research/20260907-020817_what-the-fleet-spends-on-knowing-it-is-green.md). Every second
# a `--scoped` pass saves comes from one row of tools/fixtures/s/standing_equipment_scope_map.sh,
# and until this rung nobody could say which rows earned their keep or which unwritten row would
# earn the most. That paper named the arithmetic -- a row is worth its guard's cost multiplied by
# one minus its touch rate -- and left it unbuilt. Both factors were already on disk.
#
# WHAT IS GATED, and why exactly these three. Nothing but the runner read the scope map until now,
# so faults in that file had no reader at all, and each fails SILENTLY IN THE SAFE-LOOKING
# DIRECTION. A row naming a guard the roster does not seat does nothing: the runner looks the guard
# up, finds no row, and runs it -- so a typo reads exactly like coverage while buying a full run
# every pass. A second row under one name is the same fault wearing the runner's first-match lookup
# (`{ print; exit }`), where the second row is dead text. The third is the dangerous one: a row
# naming LESS than its guard gates SKIPS REAL WORK, and the map's own header records thirteen rows
# repaired by a hand on 20260906 for exactly that. Every witness asserts on its own
# `<name>_control.sh`, so a row that cannot see that file is under-named by the map's own rule.
# All three are held at ZERO. A guard with no control at that name is counted apart and gated on
# nothing, since a naming convention is not a law.
#
# WHAT IS REPORTED RATHER THAN GATED: every cost, every touch rate, and every saving. None of them
# is a defect. A guard that is slow is a guard doing work, and gating a cost would red the tree for
# having a thorough check.
#
# THE BASIS, NAMED HONESTLY. A touch rate here is per COMMIT, where a real scoped pass diffs a
# receipt head several commits back plus every uncommitted path. So the rate is a FLOOR on how
# often a guard is really reached and the saving a CEILING on what its row really saves. That is
# the right basis for ranking rows against each other, which is what this is for, and the wrong
# basis for promising a wall-clock number. Merges are read past, since a merge's own diff is empty
# and counting one would deflate every rate by the same wrong amount.
#
# WHAT IS PROVEN, on metal, by tools/fixtures/s/standing_equipment_scope_rank_control.sh -- fifty
# behaviors, in a git repository the control builds and throws away.
#   The MATCHER first, because it is the piece two programs share: this scan and
#     `standing_equipment_run.sh --scoped`, which sources the same tools/fixtures/s/scope_match.sh.
#     A room word reaches its room and stops at the room's own name; an exact path is not a prefix;
#     a glob reaches, and its `*` crosses a slash, which is what `case` gives and therefore what
#     the map has always meant. Two spellings of that question would let this scan price a skip the
#     runner never takes.
#   All three gates planted and then LIFTED, so a refusal cannot be mistaken for a guard stuck shut.
#   A cost nobody measured reads UNKNOWN rather than zero, stays out of every sum, and stays out of
#     the ranking. On this pier that is 56 guards -- the whole cadence tier, which has never
#     recorded a run here -- so a zero printed there would read as "costs nothing" for the most
#     expensive guards in the tree.
#   THE LOAD-BEARING LEG is a NONZERO rate on planted history, shown beside a copy with the reach
#     pass stripped out. The first draft of the touch pass used one awk name as both an array and a
#     scalar; awk refused the row it reached AFTER every summary line had printed, so each rate
#     read 0.000 against a table that looked perfectly healthy and each row appeared to save its
#     whole cost. A meter that is quietly always zero passes every welcome leg ever written for it.
#
# WHAT IS NOT PROVEN. Whether a map row is the RIGHT row for its guard. The map's own header says
# that judgment lives in a reader's head -- a row follows the guard's GATED readings, so an
# advisory ratchet leaves the watch-set where it is -- and nothing here reads a witness to check it.
# This rung proves the map agrees with the roster and prices what the map already does.
#
# Style: context/GAUGE_STYLE.md - Design: active-designing/20260825-173153_reprove-only-what-moved.md
#
# Run from the repository root:
#   rishi/bin/rishi run tools/s/standing_equipment_scope_rank_witness.rish

say "scope-rank: Language EN -- a map row is worth its guard's cost times the passes it skips."
say "scope-rank: Style Gauge, Meter -- every number carries its basis, and the basis is per commit."
say "scope-rank: Lens TAME -- bound the window at the edge, and say where each number came from."

# THE WINDOW HERE IS SMALL ON PURPOSE. All three gates are window-independent -- they compare the
# map against the roster and against each guard's own control, and read no history at all. Only the
# RANKING costs, and its cost is unique-paths times mapped-rows: 40 commits reads in about ten
# seconds where 120 takes thirty, for a ranking that orders the same rows. A hand wanting a full
# day's basis runs the scan directly with `--window 120 --list`.
let scan = run ["sh" "tools/fixtures/s/standing_equipment_scope_rank.sh" "--window" "40"]
say scan.out
assert scan.ok else "scope-rank: the scope map must agree with the roster it names"
assert scan.out contains "orphan_map_rows=0" else "scope-rank: a map row naming an unseated guard is dead text that reads like coverage"
assert scan.out contains "duplicate_map_rows=0" else "scope-rank: the runner's lookup stops at the first row, so a second under one name is dead text"
assert scan.out contains "rows_missing_control=0" else "scope-rank: a row blind to its own control names less than its guard gates, which skips real work"
assert scan.out contains "verdict=ok" else "scope-rank: the scan must balance before it is believed"
say "field GREEN -- every map row names a guard the roster seats, exactly once"

let control = run ["sh" "tools/fixtures/s/standing_equipment_scope_rank_control.sh"]
say control.out
assert control.ok else "scope-rank: the control must complete -- read its own lines"

# The matcher, which two programs share.
assert control.out contains "OK   room_word_reaches_its_room" else "scope-rank: a word ending in / must reach its whole room"
assert control.out contains "OK   room_word_stops_at_the_room" else "scope-rank: caravan/ must not reach caravanserai/"
assert control.out contains "OK   room_word_is_not_the_room_itself" else "scope-rank: a room word reaches what is inside the room"
assert control.out contains "OK   exact_path_reaches_itself" else "scope-rank: a bare path must reach exactly itself"
assert control.out contains "OK   exact_path_is_not_a_prefix" else "scope-rank: a bare path must not reach a longer name beginning with it"
assert control.out contains "OK   glob_word_reaches" else "scope-rank: a shell glob must reach what the shell says it reaches"
assert control.out contains "OK   glob_star_crosses_a_slash" else "scope-rank: case gives * across a slash, which is what the map has always meant"
assert control.out contains "OK   row_takes_the_second_word" else "scope-rank: a row reaches when ANY of its words does"
assert control.out contains "OK   row_reaches_nothing_when_empty" else "scope-rank: a row with no words has no claim on any change"
assert control.out contains "OK   row_refuses_an_unreached_path" else "scope-rank: a row must refuse a path none of its words reaches"
assert control.out contains "OK   any_finds_a_hit_in_a_list" else "scope-rank: a row must reach a list holding one path it watches"
assert control.out contains "OK   any_refuses_a_list_it_cannot_reach" else "scope-rank: a row must refuse a list holding nothing it watches"
assert control.out contains "OK   any_refuses_an_empty_list" else "scope-rank: an empty changed set reaches nothing"
assert control.out contains "OK   any_refuses_an_absent_list" else "scope-rank: an absent list must refuse rather than read as a hit"

# The arithmetic, on a repository the control builds.
assert control.out contains "OK   commits_read" else "scope-rank: the window must read the commits it says it read"
assert control.out contains "OK   static_counted" else "scope-rank: a mapped guard must be counted as mapped"
assert control.out contains "OK   unmapped_counted" else "scope-rank: a guard with no row must be counted as unmapped"
assert control.out contains "OK   touch_rate_nonzero" else "scope-rank: a guard whose room moved must read a NONZERO rate -- the reading that was silently zero"
assert control.out contains "OK   touch_rate_of_a_quieter_guard" else "scope-rank: two guards touched at different rates must read differently"
assert control.out contains "OK   touch_rate_zero_when_unreached" else "scope-rank: a guard nothing reached must read zero"
assert control.out contains "OK   saving_is_cost_times_one_minus_rate" else "scope-rank: the saving must be the product the paper named"
assert control.out contains "OK   saving_of_the_quieter_guard" else "scope-rank: the product must hold at a second rate"
assert control.out contains "OK   quiet_row_saves_its_whole_cost" else "scope-rank: a row nothing reaches saves its guard's whole cost"
assert control.out contains "OK   ranked_by_saving_descending" else "scope-rank: the ranking must lead with the row that saves most"
assert control.out contains "OK   static_saving_summed" else "scope-rank: the total must be the sum of the rows"
assert control.out contains "OK   unmapped_ranked_by_cost" else "scope-rank: an unmapped guard runs every pass, so its cost is the prize for mapping it"
assert control.out contains "OK   unmapped_cost_summed" else "scope-rank: the unmapped total must be the sum of unmapped costs"
assert control.out contains "OK   mapped_guard_absent_from_unmapped" else "scope-rank: a guard must stand in one ranking, never both"

# A cost nobody measured.
assert control.out contains "OK   cost_unknown_counted" else "scope-rank: a guard with no run-card row must be counted unknown"
assert control.out contains "OK   cost_known_counted" else "scope-rank: the known count must be the denominator a reader needs"
assert control.out contains "OK   unknown_cost_left_out_of_the_sum" else "scope-rank: an unknown cost must not be summed as zero"
assert control.out contains "OK   unknown_cost_absent_from_the_ranking" else "scope-rank: a guard of unknown cost cannot be ranked by cost"

# Both gates, each planted and then lifted.
assert control.out contains "OK   orphan_row_bitten" else "scope-rank: a map row naming no seated guard must red"
assert control.out contains "OK   orphan_row_counted" else "scope-rank: the orphan count must name how many rows are dead"
assert control.out contains "OK   orphan_row_named" else "scope-rank: an orphan must be named, so it can be fixed rather than hunted"
assert control.out contains "OK   orphan_row_lifted" else "scope-rank: lifting the orphan must return the verdict to ok, so no bypass exists"
assert control.out contains "OK   duplicate_row_bitten" else "scope-rank: a second row under one name must red"
assert control.out contains "OK   duplicate_row_counted" else "scope-rank: the duplicate count must name how many names are doubled"
assert control.out contains "OK   duplicate_row_named" else "scope-rank: a duplicate must be named"
assert control.out contains "OK   duplicate_row_lifted" else "scope-rank: lifting the duplicate must return the verdict to ok"
assert control.out contains "OK   unreached_control_bitten" else "scope-rank: a row that cannot see its own control must red"
assert control.out contains "OK   unreached_control_counted" else "scope-rank: the count must name how many rows are blind to their controls"
assert control.out contains "OK   unreached_control_named" else "scope-rank: the blind row must be named, so its watch word can be written"
assert control.out contains "OK   reached_control_lifted" else "scope-rank: adding the watch word must return the verdict to ok, so no bypass exists"
assert control.out contains "OK   reached_control_counted_zero" else "scope-rank: the count must fall to zero when the row is repaired"
assert control.out contains "OK   guards_without_a_control_counted_apart" else "scope-rank: a naming convention is not a law, so a guard with no such file is counted apart"

# The bounds and the print.
assert control.out contains "OK   top_bounds_the_print" else "scope-rank: --top must bound the print"
assert control.out contains "OK   top_names_the_remainder" else "scope-rank: a truncated table with no remainder line reads as a whole one"
assert control.out contains "OK   list_prints_them_all" else "scope-rank: --list must print every row"
assert control.out contains "OK   window_zero_refused" else "scope-rank: a window of zero commits measures nothing"
assert control.out contains "OK   window_past_the_bound_refused" else "scope-rank: the reach pass is unique paths times rows, so the window is bounded at the edge"
assert control.out contains "OK   window_not_a_number_refused" else "scope-rank: a window that is not a number must refuse rather than read as one"
assert control.out contains "OK   unknown_argument_refused" else "scope-rank: an argument this scan does not know must refuse rather than be read past"

# The load-bearing leg.
assert control.out contains "OK   blind_copy_reads_every_rate_zero" else "scope-rank: a copy with the reach pass stripped must read every rate as zero"
assert control.out contains "OK   blind_copy_saves_the_whole_cost" else "scope-rank: a quietly-zero meter must be shown, since it passes every welcome leg"

assert control.out contains "OK   discovery_row_counted" else "scope-rank: a row spelling DISCOVERY must be counted as its own class"
assert control.out contains "OK   discovery_is_not_static" else "scope-rank: a DISCOVERY row has no watch-set, so it must never be priced as a static one"
assert control.out contains "OK   discovery_cost_named_apart" else "scope-rank: a DISCOVERY guard's seconds can never be claimed by any row, so they are named apart"
assert control.out contains "OK   discovery_leaves_nothing_claimable" else "scope-rank: declaring every unmapped guard DISCOVERY must leave no claimable seconds"
assert control.out contains "OK   discovery_named_in_rank_unmapped" else "scope-rank: the unmapped ranking must say which entries can never be mapped"
assert control.out contains "OK   absent_cost_claimable_again" else "scope-rank: lifting the DISCOVERY row must return its seconds to the claimable half, so no bypass exists"
assert control.out contains "OK   unmapped_total_unchanged_either_way" else "scope-rank: the split must partition the unmapped tail rather than change it"
assert control.out contains "OK   split_sums_to_the_whole" else "scope-rank: the two halves must sum to the whole, so neither is dropped nor double-counted"
assert control.out contains "OK   claimable_share_below_unmapped_share" else "scope-rank: the claimable ceiling must read below the unmapped one once any guard is declared"

assert control.out contains "faults=0" else "scope-rank: every behavior must be satisfied"
assert control.out contains "control_verdict=ok" else "scope-rank: the control must balance before it is believed"
say "the matcher and the arithmetic proven in a real repository, all three gates shown from both sides"

say "GREEN: scope-rank -- the map agrees with the roster, and every row now carries a price."
